## 4️⃣ Checklist for Ongoing Security

| ✅ Item | How to verify / implement |
|--------|----------------------------|
| **Dependencies up‑to‑date** | Run `npm audit fix` regularly; add `npm audit` as part of CI. |
| **Secrets management** | Keep `.env` out of source control (`.gitignore`). Use a secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault) in production. |
| **HTTPS** | Deploy behind TLS‑terminating reverse proxy (Nginx, Traefik) or use a cloud load balancer that enforces HTTPS. |
| **Content Security Policy** | Adjust `helmet.contentSecurityPolicy` if you ever serve HTML/JS. |
| **Input validation** | When you add POST/PUT routes, use `express-validator` or `Joi` to whitelist allowed fields. |
| **Database safety** | Use prepared statements (`pool.query('SELECT … WHERE id = $1', [id])`) or an ORM that auto‑escapes. |
| **Security testing** | Add automated OWASP ZAP or npm `npm run test:security` in CI. |
| **Monitoring & alerting** | Ship `morgan`/`winston` logs to a SIEM; set alerts on 5xx spikes. |
| **Rate‑limit critical endpoints** | Apply `express-rate-limit` per endpoint as needed. |
| **Principle of least privilege** | Run the Node process under a non‑root OS user; restrict container capabilities. |

