### Quick Summary
| OWASP Top‑10 Category | Finding | Severity | Recommendation |
|-----------------------|---------|----------|----------------|
| **A01 – Broken Access Control** | No authentication/authorization on any endpoint (e.g., `/users` returns personal e‑mail addresses). | High | Add auth guard (JWT, session, OAuth) and limit data exposure. |
| **A02 – Cryptographic Failures** | Server runs over plain HTTP; no TLS enforcement. | High | Deploy behind a TLS‑terminating reverse‑proxy (NGINX, Cloudflare) or enable HTTPS in Node for local dev. |
| **A03 – Injection** | No user‑supplied data is currently processed, but future routes could be vulnerable. | Medium | Use parameterised queries/ORM, sanitise input, add validation middleware. |
| **A04 – Insecure Design** | The API is “open‑by‑default”: anyone can enumerate users and see e‑mail addresses. | High | Follow the principle of least privilege – only expose data after auth and with proper filtering. |
| **A05 – Security Misconfiguration** | • No security‑related HTTP headers. <br>• No rate‑limiting or request size limits. <br>• `app.listen` hard‑codes port 3000. | Medium | Add Helmet, rate‑limiting, request‑size limits, configurable port via `process.env.PORT`. |
| **A06 – Vulnerable & Out‑dated Components** | No explicit version check; depends on Express (and possibly other packages) – ensure they are up‑to‑date. | Medium | Run `npm audit` regularly; lock versions in `package‑lock.json`. |
| **A07 – Identification & Authentication Failures** | Same as A01 – no auth at all. | High | Implement robust auth (JWT, OAuth2) and protect sensitive routes. |
| **A08 – Software & Data Integrity** | No integrity checks on incoming data; no CSP. | Low | Enable CSP via Helmet, use Subresource Integrity if you ever serve static assets. |
| **A09 – Logging & Monitoring** | No request logging, no error logging, and stack traces are not hidden. | Medium | Add morgan/winston, redacted error handling, and integrate with a SIEM. |
| **A10 – Server‑Side Request Forgery** | Not applicable now, but future routes that call external services should validate URLs. | Low | Validate/whitelist any outbound URLs. |

