## 3. Input Validation & Sanitisation (Future‑Proof)

When you add routes that accept **path parameters**, **query strings**, or **request bodies**, always validate them with `express-validator` (already imported above). Example for a route that creates a new user:

```js
app.post(
  '/users',
  authenticateJwt,
  body('name').isString().trim().isLength({ min: 1, max: 100 }),
  body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail(),
  body('password').isStrongPassword({ minLength: 12 }),
  validate,
  async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
      // Example: hash password, store user, return safe representation
      const hashed = await bcrypt.hash(req.body.password, 12);
      // DB insert here …
      res.status(201).json({ id: newUserId, name: req.body.name, email: req.body.email });
    } catch (err) {
      next(err);
    }
  }
