## 4. Additional OWASP‑Focused Recommendations

| OWASP Issue | Why It Matters | Quick Fix |
|-------------|----------------|-----------|
| **A01 – Broken Access Control** | Anyone can enumerate all users (including email). | Restrict `/users` to authenticated/authorized callers; return only non‑sensitive fields. |
| **A02 – Cryptographic Failures** | Data in transit could be sniffed. | Deploy behind TLS. Set `Strict-Transport-Security` header (`helmet.hsts`). |
| **A05 – Security Misconfiguration** | Default Express error pages leak stack traces. | Use the central error handler shown above; disable `x-powered-by` (`app.disable('x-powered-by')`). |
| **A06 – Vulnerable Components** | Out‑dated dependencies may contain known CVEs. | Run `npm audit fix --force` regularly; lock versions with `package-lock.json`. |
| **A07 – Authentication Failures** | No auth => data leakage. | Implement JWT or session auth (see code). |
| **A09 – Logging & Monitoring** | No visibility into attacks. | Add `morgan` (already in `server.js`) + a structured logger like `winston`; forward logs to a SIEM. |
| **A10 – SSRF** | Future endpoints that call external URLs can be abused. | Validate/whitelist any URL parameters; use `axios` with a DNS‑allowlist or `net.isIP` checks. |

