| **No input handling at all** (future endpoints might accept query/body data) | A1 – Injection, A7 – Cross‑Site Scripting (XSS) | The lack of validation means the next route you add could be vulnerable. |
| **Hard‑coded port** | A5 – Security Misconfiguration | Makes it harder to configure per‑environment (e.g., production behind reverse proxy). |
| **No error handling / stack‑trace leakage** | A6 – Vulnerable & Out‑of‑Date Components (exposes internal detail) | Uncaught errors will be sent to the client in development; in production they can leak implementation details. |
| **No logging / rate‑limit** | A10 – Insufficient Logging & Monitoring | Without request‑level logs or throttling you can’t detect abuse. |

