## 4️⃣ Checklist for Ongoing Security

| ✅ Item | How to Verify |
|--------|----------------|
| **Helmet & security headers** | `curl -I https://yourhost/health` → look for `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, etc. |
| **CORS** | `curl -I -H "Origin: evil.com" https://yourhost/users` → should return `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` only for allowed origins. |
| **Rate limiting** | Send >100 requests in 15 min from same IP; expect `429 Too Many Requests`. |
| **Input validation** | Try `/users/abc` → gets `400 Bad Request`. |
| **Authentication** | Call `/users` without `Authorization` header → `401`. |
| **HTTPS enforcement** | Access via `http://` in production → 301 → `https://`. |
| **Error handling** | Trigger an uncaught exception (e.g., `throw new Error('test')` in a dummy route) – response should be generic, stack only in logs. |
| **Dependency audit** | Run `npm audit --production` in CI; fail on high severity. |
| **Logging** | Verify logs contain request/response metadata (`combined` format). |
| **Secret management** | Check that `JWT_SECRET`, `PORT`, etc., are **not** committed to source (use `.gitignore` for `.env`). |

